# Signal-frame CFI must be recognized at the raw PC even when no function or
# symbol covers it. Use PE/COFF because ELF synthesizes symbols from .eh_frame.
# PC - 1 belongs to "previous", so retrying symbol lookup there would select
# the wrong function. The trampoline's second CFI row also describes a different
# stack layout, making it necessary to select the row at the raw PC.
# A second thread stops directly in that trampoline to exercise frame zero.
# A third thread returns into a named trampoline at a CFI row transition, where
# backing up the PC would select the preceding row and lose the caller.

# REQUIRES: x86

# RUN: mkdir -p %t.dir
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/signal-frame-no-symbol.exe.yaml -o %t.dir/signal-frame-no-symbol.exe
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/signal-frame-no-symbol.dmp.yaml -o %t.dir/signal-frame-no-symbol.dmp
# RUN: %lldb -O "log enable -f %t.log 'lldb' unwind" \
# RUN:   %t.dir/signal-frame-no-symbol.exe -c %t.dir/signal-frame-no-symbol.dmp \
# RUN:   -s %s -o exit | FileCheck %s
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UNWIND < %t.log

image lookup -v -a 0x140001fff
# CHECK-LABEL: image lookup -v -a 0x140001fff
# CHECK: Symbol: {{.*}}name="previous"

image lookup -v -a 0x140002000
# CHECK-LABEL: image lookup -v -a 0x140002000
# CHECK: Address: signal-frame-no-symbol.exe[0x0000000140002000]
# CHECK-NOT: Function:
# CHECK-NOT: Symbol:

thread backtrace -u 1
# CHECK-LABEL: thread backtrace -u 1
# CHECK: frame #0: 0x0000000140001000 signal-frame-no-symbol.exe`leaf
# CHECK-NEXT: frame #1: 0x0000000140002000 signal-frame-no-symbol.exe`{{$}}
# CHECK-NEXT: frame #2: 0x0000000140001010 signal-frame-no-symbol.exe`caller
# CHECK-NOT: frame #3:

thread backtrace -u 2
# CHECK-LABEL: thread backtrace -u 2
# CHECK: frame #0: 0x0000000140002000 signal-frame-no-symbol.exe`{{$}}
# CHECK-NEXT: frame #1: 0x0000000140001010 signal-frame-no-symbol.exe`caller
# CHECK-NOT: frame #2:

image lookup -v -a 0x140002021
# CHECK-LABEL: image lookup -v -a 0x140002021
# CHECK: Symbol: {{.*}}name="tramp"

thread backtrace -u 3
# CHECK-LABEL: thread backtrace -u 3
# CHECK: frame #0: 0x0000000140001000 signal-frame-no-symbol.exe`leaf
# CHECK-NEXT: frame #1: 0x0000000140002021 signal-frame-no-symbol.exe`tramp + 1
# CHECK-NEXT: frame #2: 0x0000000140001010 signal-frame-no-symbol.exe`caller
# CHECK-NOT: frame #3:

# Check that the unwinder itself failed symbol lookup but still used the
# signal-frame CFI and its first row.
# UNWIND: with pc value of 0x140002000, no symbol/function name is known.
# UNWIND: This frame is marked as a trap handler via its UnwindPlan
# UNWIND: Using full unwind plan 'eh_frame CFI'
# UNWIND: active row: 0x0000000140002000: CFA=rsp+16 => rip=[CFA-8]

# The named trampoline must keep the raw PC and use the row starting there,
# rather than the preceding row with CFA=rsp+24.
# UNWIND: with pc value of 0x140002021, symbol name is 'tramp'
# UNWIND-NOT: Backing up the pc value of 0x140002021
# UNWIND: Using full unwind plan 'eh_frame CFI'
# UNWIND: active row: 0x0000000140002021: CFA=rsp+16 => rip=[CFA-8]
